{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/012-adirondacks-round-1/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Wood Times"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"2f00da69-bf3d-583c-b94f-06a3c94fc0a1","excerpt":"There’s something deeply satisfying about building furniture you can actually sit in. Adirondack chairs had been on my project list since day one.  Iconic…","html":"<p>There’s something deeply satisfying about building furniture you can actually sit in. Adirondack chairs had been on my project list since day one.  Iconic design, comfortable for lounging, and a great test of skills across multiple techniques.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/669cd/plans.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Plans\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/f058b/plans.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/c26ae/plans.png 158w,\n/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/6bdcf/plans.png 315w,\n/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/f058b/plans.png 630w,\n/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/40601/plans.png 945w,\n/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/78612/plans.png 1260w,\n/static/c18b4bca99ca026b6b5f3b6a73c50e75/669cd/plans.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>I found a solid set of plans that called for about 20 board feet of lumber per chair, carriage bolts for the structural connections, and plugs to cover the screw holes. The tool list was manageable: bandsaw for curves, drill bits for precision holes and plugs, and lots of sanding.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/669cd/lumber.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Lumber\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/f058b/lumber.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/c26ae/lumber.png 158w,\n/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/6bdcf/lumber.png 315w,\n/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/f058b/lumber.png 630w,\n/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/40601/lumber.png 945w,\n/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/78612/lumber.png 1260w,\n/static/f194ae0b3a4dc3fea078f2c6efe5d3af/669cd/lumber.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Cypress was the wood of choice for these outdoor chairs. Naturally rot-resistant and stable in changing weather, it’s the traditional material for porch furniture in the South. I marked up the boards for efficient cuts.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/669cd/assembly.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Assembly\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/f058b/assembly.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/c26ae/assembly.png 158w,\n/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/6bdcf/assembly.png 315w,\n/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/f058b/assembly.png 630w,\n/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/40601/assembly.png 945w,\n/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/78612/assembly.png 1260w,\n/static/1a4f160d40de26b7d2594624aaa6843e/669cd/assembly.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Dad came over to help with the build and have a couple of beers (aftrer we were done milling for the day). The chair frame came together quickly once we had a rhythm going.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/669cd/complete_shop.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Complete Shop\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/f058b/complete_shop.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/c26ae/complete_shop.png 158w,\n/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/6bdcf/complete_shop.png 315w,\n/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/f058b/complete_shop.png 630w,\n/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/40601/complete_shop.png 945w,\n/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/78612/complete_shop.png 1260w,\n/static/0c3ddccfd2f4c8f855016b243ce3e498/669cd/complete_shop.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The first chair complete and ready for a test sit. The curved back slats and wide armrests are what make an Adirondack an Adirondack. Plenty of room for a drink on that armrest.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/493ac/pair_outside.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Pair Outside\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/f058b/pair_outside.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/c26ae/pair_outside.png 158w,\n/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/6bdcf/pair_outside.png 315w,\n/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/f058b/pair_outside.png 630w,\n/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/40601/pair_outside.png 945w,\n/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/78612/pair_outside.png 1260w,\n/static/ba2c375f2ebe4fe31e6aaefec4b8b753/493ac/pair_outside.png 4032w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Chairs come in pairs, of course. Seeing them sitting on the patio, ready for actual use, was incredibly rewarding. These weren’t just shop projects anymore; they were furniture that would get used for years to come.</p>\n<p>Round one complete, but definitely not the last Adirondacks I’d build.</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"Adirondacks Round 1","date":"July 29, 2018","description":null}},"previous":{"fields":{"slug":"/011-shop-upgrade-3/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Shop Upgrade 3 - Finding the Flow"}},"next":{"fields":{"slug":"/013-spokeshave-kit/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Spokeshave Kit"}}},"pageContext":{"id":"2f00da69-bf3d-583c-b94f-06a3c94fc0a1","previousPostId":"954691f1-dfb0-5b38-81bf-4dd504e4722f","nextPostId":"7a931caa-4614-5099-9c97-c6ff1001db29"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2841359383"],"slicesMap":{}}